  "problem": "Suppose that $X$ is a continuous random variable. For which of the following transformations can the change-of-variables method be applied to find the probability density function of $Y?$\n\nI. $Y={X}^{5}+1,$ where $X\\in (-1,1)$\n\nII. $Y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2X,$ where $X\\in (0,\\frac{\\pi }{2})$\n\nIII. $Y=1-{X}^{4},$ where $X\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$",
